will be the most dangerous to hold onto. So, I will drop B8.\n\n\n", "output": "Evaluation: The hand is aiming for \"Thirteen Orphans\" (13 Yao), currently holding 10 valid tiles (F1, F2, F3, F4, J1, J2, J3, J3, B1, W9) and needs W1, T1, T9, B9. The tiles W4, W8, B2, B8 are unnecessary for this pattern. 13 Orphans is a high-scoring pattern (88 points) and is the most viable path given the hand structure (pair of J3 is already secured).\nReason: Among the useless tiles (W4, W8, B2, B8), B2 and W4 have been played previously by the player or the next player, making them safer tiles to hold for defensive purposes later in the game. B8 is completely unshown (4 left), making it potentially dangerous to discard later if opponents approach a winning hand; therefore, it is strategically better to discard B8 now (\"Saki-giri\") while opponents are likely still developing their hands (indicated by their recent discards of Bamboo tiles like B5, B6, B9).\nAnswer: Play B8"}
